A.mc("e2-c7-standard-1-check","c7-1-core","A river flood leaves mud beside the channel while its mouth builds into a lake. Which pair identifies the two deposits?",["*Floodplain beside the channel; delta at the mouth|Overbank mud builds a floodplain; slowing at the mouth builds a delta.", "Delta beside the channel; floodplain at the mouth|This reverses the locations of a delta and a floodplain.", "Alluvial fan beside the channel; beach at the mouth|A fan needs a mountain-front spreading setting; the stated mouth is a river-built delta.", "Channel bar beside the channel; lagoon at the mouth|The first deposit is outside the channel and the second grows from river-delivered sediment."],"Overbank mud builds a floodplain; slowing at the mouth builds a delta.",["TB7:7.1"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S1"], "media": [{"kind": "img", "src": "assets/figures/chapter7-standard/7.1-p3-Im2.png", "alt": "Photographic or diagram evidence A from the course source; inspect the visible properties.", "cap": "Figure A · Exploring Geology 7.1 · PDF p3 · unchanged source geometry."}], "sourceFigure": true});
A.teach("e2-c7-standard-1-write","c7-1-core","Contrast a river floodplain with a delta. State where each forms and the process depositing its sediment.","A floodplain borders a river and receives overbank mud and sand during floods. A delta builds at a river mouth where the current slows on entering standing water.",["Locates the floodplain beside a river.", "Explains deposition by overbank flooding.", "Locates the delta at a river mouth.", "Explains deposition as flow enters standing water and slows."],["TB7:7.1"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S1"], "focusedWriting": true});
