A.mc("e2-c7-standard-2-check","c7-2-core","Two nearby shallow-water sites differ: one is muddy behind a barrier, the other has clear water and growing coral. Which interpretation fits?",["*Lagoon behind the barrier; reef in the clear water|Protection supports a lagoon; growing coral supports a reef.", "Tidal flat behind the barrier; beach in the clear water|No repeated exposure is supplied for the first site, and living coral is not a beach deposit.", "Delta behind the barrier; lagoon in the clear water|The stem does not supply a river-mouth body; growing coral identifies a reef.", "Reef behind the barrier; open shelf in the clear water|The first site is muddy protected water; the second specifically contains a growing reef."],"Protection supports a lagoon; growing coral supports a reef.",["TB7:7.2"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S2"], "media": [{"kind": "img", "src": "assets/figures/chapter7-standard/7.2-p2-Im2.png", "alt": "Photographic or diagram evidence A from the course source; inspect the visible properties.", "cap": "Figure A · Exploring Geology 7.2 · PDF p2 · unchanged source geometry."}, {"kind": "img", "src": "assets/figures/chapter7-standard/7.2-p2-Im1.png", "alt": "Photographic or diagram evidence B from the course source; inspect the visible properties.", "cap": "Figure B · Exploring Geology 7.2 · PDF p2 · unchanged source geometry."}], "sourceFigure": true});
A.teach("e2-c7-standard-2-write","c7-2-core","Distinguish a lagoon from a reef. Give one source-supported sediment or formation clue for each.","A lagoon is sheltered water behind a barrier or reef and can trap land-derived mud. A reef is a framework constructed by organisms in suitable shallow, warm, clear water and supplies carbonate remains.",["Defines lagoon as protected water.", "Gives mud or another supported lagoon sediment.", "Defines reef as an organism-built structure.", "Gives a supported reef growth or carbonate clue."],["TB7:7.2"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S2"], "focusedWriting": true});
