A.mc("e2-c7-standard-4-check","c7-4-core","A sample contains large rounded pebbles mixed with fine sand and clay. Which description is supported?",["*Rounded clasts in a poorly sorted mixture|Rounded edges concern shape; the wide size range means poor sorting.", "Angular clasts in a well-sorted mixture|The stem gives rounded rather than angular edges and multiple sizes.", "Rounded clasts in a single-size mixture|The fine and coarse particles contradict a single-size mixture.", "Angular clasts in a single-size mixture|Both the stated edge shape and the broad size range contradict this choice."],"Rounded edges concern shape; the wide size range means poor sorting.",["TB7:7.4"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S4"], "media": [{"kind": "img", "src": "assets/figures/chapter7-standard/7.4-p6-Im3.png", "alt": "Photographic or diagram evidence A from the course source; inspect the visible properties.", "cap": "Figure A · Exploring Geology 7.4 · PDF p6 · unchanged source geometry."}], "sourceFigure": true});
A.teach("e2-c7-standard-4-write","c7-4-core","List the four controls on transported sediment named in this section. Explain why strong flow alone cannot predict the largest clast present.","The controls are slope steepness, current strength, sediment supply and transport agent. Strong flow can move large particles only if that size of material is supplied; an absent boulder source cannot be inferred from current strength alone.",["Lists slope steepness.", "Lists current strength.", "Lists sediment supply and transporting agent.", "Explains that transport is limited by available material."],["TB7:7.4"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S4"], "focusedWriting": true});
