A.mc("e2-c7-standard-5-check","c7-5-core","Buried sand becomes thinner, then minerals grow between its solid grains. What sequence occurred?",["*Compaction followed by cementation|Packing reduces thickness; minerals then precipitate to bind the grains.", "Cementation followed by compaction|This reverses packing first and mineral binding second.", "Transport followed by deposition|These move and settle sediment; they do not explain the stated burial packing and pore minerals.", "Dissolution followed by abrasion|Those remove or scrape material rather than describing the stated grain packing and mineral growth."],"Packing reduces thickness; minerals then precipitate to bind the grains.",["TB7:7.5"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S5"]});
A.teach("e2-c7-standard-5-write","c7-5-core","Contrast compaction with cementation. Name all four common natural cements identified in the section.","Compaction packs solid grains together and expels pore fluid. Cementation precipitates minerals in pores to bind grains. The four common cements are calcite, silica, clay minerals and iron oxides.",["Explains packing and pore reduction in compaction.", "Explains mineral binding in cementation.", "Names calcite and silica.", "Names clay minerals and iron oxides."],["TB7:7.5"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S5"], "focusedWriting": true});
