A.teach("e2-c7-standard-10-write","c7-10-core","Contrast siltstone, shale and mudstone using grain size and splitting behavior.","Siltstone is dominated by silt-sized grains. Shale is very fine grained and characteristically splits into thin chips or flakes. Mudstone or mudrock is a general rock made from silt and clay; mudstone need not show shale’s thin splitting.",["Defines siltstone by silt-sized grains.", "Identifies shale as very fine grained.", "States shale’s thin splitting behavior.", "Explains mudstone/mudrock and the splitting distinction."],["TB7:7.10"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S10"], "focusedWriting": true});
