A.mc("e2-c7-standard-12-check","c7-12-core","At one fixed site, beach sand is followed by lagoon mud and then reef limestone in this source model. What changed?",["*Shoreline migration landward during transgression|Increasingly offshore environments pass over the fixed location as the sea advances.", "Shoreline migration seaward during regression|Regression produces the opposite environmental trend in this source example.", "A stationary beach with unchanged sediment supply|Lagoon and reef conditions at the same site require environmental change in this model.", "Repeated channel flooding without marine encroachment|That does not explain the progression into an offshore reef in the supplied coastal model."],"Increasingly offshore environments pass over the fixed location as the sea advances.",["TB7:7.12"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S12"], "media": [{"kind": "img", "src": "assets/figures/chapter7-standard/7.12-p2-Im1.png", "alt": "Photographic or diagram evidence A from the course source; inspect the visible properties.", "cap": "Figure A · Exploring Geology 7.12 · PDF p2 · unchanged source geometry."}, {"kind": "img", "src": "assets/figures/chapter7-standard/7.12-p4-Im1.png", "alt": "Photographic or diagram evidence B from the course source; inspect the visible properties.", "cap": "Figure B · Exploring Geology 7.12 · PDF p4 · unchanged source geometry."}], "sourceFigure": true});
A.teach("e2-c7-standard-12-write","c7-12-core","At a fixed site in this source model, compare the transgressive and regressive rock successions and the direction of shoreline migration.","Transgression moves the shoreline landward and leaves beach sandstone, lagoon mudstone and reef limestone upward. Regression moves it seaward and can leave limestone, mudstone and sandstone upward. The sequence reflects migrating facies at one location, not every coast’s mandatory rock order.",["Names landward migration in transgression.", "Gives the source transgressive succession.", "Names seaward migration in regression.", "Gives the regressive succession and preserves the source-model limit."],["TB7:7.12"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S12"], "focusedWriting": true});
