A.mc("e2-c7-standard-13-check","c7-13-core","In the source examples, cross beds dip left and flat river pebbles lean right. Which flow direction makes both consistent?",["*Flow toward the left|Cross beds slope down-current; imbricated clasts lean against flow.", "Flow toward the right|This reverses both supplied directional indicators.", "Equal proof of flow in both directions|The two structures here support one direction rather than symmetric waves.", "No possible current could produce both|The two observations are consistent under the source relationships."],"Cross beds slope down-current; imbricated clasts lean against flow.",["TB7:7.13"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S13"], "media": [{"kind": "img", "src": "assets/figures/chapter7-standard/7.13-p7-Im3.png", "alt": "Photographic or diagram evidence A from the course source; inspect the visible properties.", "cap": "Figure A · Exploring Geology 7.13 · PDF p7 · unchanged source geometry."}, {"kind": "img", "src": "assets/figures/chapter7-standard/7.13-p7-Im2.png", "alt": "Photographic or diagram evidence B from the course source; inspect the visible properties.", "cap": "Figure B · Exploring Geology 7.13 · PDF p7 · unchanged source geometry."}], "sourceFigure": true});
A.teach("e2-c7-standard-13-write","c7-13-core","For the source examples, compare flow directions shown by cross beds and imbricated clasts. Explain why symmetric ripples need a different interpretation.","Cross beds slope down-current. Imbricated river clasts lean against the current. Symmetric ripples can form from back-and-forth waves and do not by themselves specify a single net current direction.",["States the cross-bed relation.", "States the opposite imbrication relation.", "Connects symmetric ripples to oscillating waves.", "Avoids claiming one net direction from symmetry alone."],["TB7:7.13"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S13"], "focusedWriting": true});
