A.mc("e2-c7-standard-14-check","c7-14-core","A porous sandstone has no documented source rock or effective seal. What can be concluded from porosity alone?",["*Storage space is present; petroleum remains unproven|Pores provide space; generation, migration and retention require further evidence.", "A petroleum source is established by pore abundance|Porosity is not evidence that organic material generated oil or gas.", "An effective seal is established by pore abundance|Reservoir pore space does not demonstrate the overlying trapping seal.", "A producing oil field is established by pore abundance|Commercial accumulation cannot be concluded from porosity alone."],"Pores provide space; generation, migration and retention require further evidence.",["TB7:7.14"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S14"]});
A.teach("e2-c7-standard-14-write","c7-14-core","Distinguish a petroleum source rock, a reservoir and a trapping condition. Explain why porosity alone is insufficient evidence of petroleum.","Organic-rich source rock generates petroleum. A reservoir provides storage in pores or fractures. Trapping geometry with an effective seal can retain migrating petroleum. Porosity alone establishes space, without proving generation, supply or retention.",["Identifies the generating source.", "Explains reservoir storage.", "Explains retention by a trap and seal.", "States why porosity does not prove petroleum."],["TB7:7.14"],{"examId": "exam2", "mock": false, "topics": ["E2C7S14"], "focusedWriting": true});
